Z||000002||recluse||11-06-2001||10:42 PM||||I think its because of the pressure that builds up under the front end at high speeds.  A front hood scoop should help reduce pressure. Ive only had it happen twice, once at 100 and once at 105, but Ive had it alot faster and they stayed down. It just depends on things like wind, steep hills, gravitational pull of the moon, etc...||||reg||1
